From: iAmMichaelConnor <mike@aztec.foundation>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:27:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat!: discover note nonces in both nonce domains

Private note hashes are made unique in private with their index among the tx's
private note hashes, revertible or not. Note hashes emitted in public use
DOM_SEP__PUBLIC_NOTE_HASH_NONCE with their index in the tx's note hashes.

- nonce discovery tries every index in both nonce domains
- the PXE's kernel-less simulation uniquifies every private note hash once,
  before splitting by revertibility, matching the private kernel
- computePublicNoteHashNonce in stdlib
- the new separator joins aztec-nr's domain-separator collision test

